{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-1","title":"Mark 15:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jesus brought bound, and accused before Pilate. 6 Upon the clamour of the common people, the murderer Barabbas is loosed, and Jesus delivered up to be crucified. 16 He is crowned with thorns, spit on, and mocked; 21 faints in bearing his cross; 27 hangs between two thieves; 29 suffers the triumphing reproaches of the Jews; 39 but is confessed by the centurion to be the Son of God; 42 and is honourably buried by Joseph.</p>\n<p>straightway. Ps 2:2; Mt 27:1,2; Lu 22:66; Ac 4:5,6,25-28 and delivered. 10:33,34; Mt 20:18,19; Lu 18:32,33; 23:1,2-5; Joh 18:28-38; Ac 3:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-2","title":"Mark 15:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Mt 2:2; 27:11; Lu 23:3; Joh 18:33-37; 19:19-22; 1Ti 6:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-3","title":"Mark 15:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the chief. Mt 27:12; Lu 23:2-5; Joh 18:29-31; 19:6,7,12 but. 5; 14:60,61; Isa 53:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-4","title":"Mark 15:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Answerest. Mt 26:62; 27:13; Joh 19:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-5","title":"Mark 15:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Jesus. Isa 53:7; Joh 19:9 Pilate. Ps 71:7; Isa 8:18; Zec 3:8; Mt 27:14; 1Co 4:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-15-6","title":"Mark 15:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Mt 26:2,5; 27:15; Lu 23:16,17; Joh 18:39,40; Ac 24:27; 25:9</p>"}